  questionAnswers:
  - questions: "What does the following traffic sign mean? \U0001F6AB\U0001F697  "
    options:
    - Entry permitted for private vehicles only
    - ' No entry for motor vehicles'
    - Entry permitted for public vehicles
    - Entry permitted for two-wheeled vehicles only
    answers: ' No entry for motor vehicles'
  - questions: What should you do when approaching a crosswalk with a pedestrian
      intending to cross?
    options:
    - Slow down and proceed carefully
    - Honk to warn the pedestrian
    - Stop and allow them to cross
    - Carefully overtake the pedestrian
    answers: Stop and allow them to cross
  - questions: What is the maximum speed allowed on an urban road if not specified
      otherwise?
    options:
    - 60 km/h
    - 40 km/h
    - 70 km/h
    - 50 km/h
    answers: 50 km/h
  - questions: What is the role of the ABS system in a vehicle?
    options:
    - To save fuel
    - To prevent wheel lock during braking
    - To improve vehicle speed
    - To activate the airbags
    answers: To prevent wheel lock during braking
  - questions: How can you identify a warning sign?
    options:
    - Blue circle with a symbol
    - Green square with text
    - Triangle with a red border
    - Yellow rectangle with a black stripe
    answers: Triangle with a red border
  - questions: "What is your obligation when you see an approaching emergency vehicle
      with flashing lights? \U0001F691"
    options:
    - Continue as normal
    - Stop on the right and clear the way
    - Slow down and drive on the shoulder
    - Speed up to avoid hindrance
    answers: Stop on the right and clear the way
  - questions: What does a double solid line mean?
    options:
    - Overtaking is allowed with caution
    - Crossing is allowed only for a left turn
    - Crossing or overtaking is prohibited
    - Overtaking is allowed only for two-wheeled vehicles
    answers: Crossing or overtaking is prohibited
  - questions: What is the correct way to check tire pressure?
    options:
    - After driving for 10 minutes
    - When the tires are warm
    - When the tires are cold
    - Only at a gas station
    answers: When the tires are cold
